## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** Cat Jam
- **Short description:** A provenance-hidden OpenCode Zen stealth reasoning model offered free for a limited preview, announced by @opencode on 2026-10-13 as "very fast — built for agentic coding." Maker undisclosed; community speculation (unconfirmed) points to Reflection's Beam line.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen (`opencode/cat-jam`, also listed as `cat-jam-free` on models.dev / pi.dev; `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1`, OpenAI-compatible). No vendor attribution or public endpoint outside Zen.
- **Release / knowledge:** listed in the Zen registry 2026-10-12/13; knowledge cutoff unknown.
- **IDs:** `opencode/cat-jam`, `opencode/cat-jam-free`.
- **Context window:** 262,144 tokens with 131,072 max output (pi.dev, aifree.dev); Command Code lists 1.05M — a conflicting figure, treated as unconfirmed.
- **Modalities:** text-only (no image/attachment input reported); reasoning with low/medium/high/xhigh/max effort, tool calls, and structured JSON output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-18):** Free — $0 input / $0 output / $0 cache read (limited stealth-preview period; no announced end date).
- **Architecture:** not disclosed (parameters, MoE/dense, weights and license all unknown).

